                                 RECITALS

WHEREAS the Licensor, being possessed of the Work and of no particular desire
to be remunerated therefor in coin, specie, scrip or any instrument negotiable
or otherwise; and WHEREAS it is nonetheless considered meet and proper that
the enjoyment of the Work should occasion some modest increase in the sum of
unlooked-for refreshment obtaining among the public at large; NOW, THEREFORE,
the Work is made available upon, and only upon, the terms hereinafter appearing.

1.  DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

    1.1  In this Licence, unless the context otherwise requires or the
         contrary intention appears (and it shall not lightly be presumed to
         appear):

         (a)  "the Work" means the software, documentation and associated
              materials to which this Licence is annexed, save always for the
              Excluded Materials;

         (b)  "Licensee" means any person, natural or juristic, who Uses the
              Work, and "You" and "Your" shall be construed accordingly,
              mutatis mutandis;

         (c)  "Use" means to compile, flash, execute, copy, adapt, distribute
              or otherwise derive benefit from the Work, whether or not any
              drone be thereby observed to race, and cognate expressions
              shall bear a corresponding meaning;

         (d)  "Juice" means not less than one (1) sealed vessel of potable,
              non-intoxicating liquid refreshment of a kind customarily
              dispensed by vending apparatus, convenience establishments or
              equivalent purveyors, it being acknowledged for the avoidance
              of doubt that tea, coffee, carbonated preparations and sports
              drinks are Juice for the purposes hereof notwithstanding that
              they are not, botanically speaking, juice;

         (e)  "Stranger" means a natural person in respect of whom the
              Licensee stands, immediately prior to the Conveyance, in no
              relation of acquaintance, kinship, employment, friendship,
              enmity or mutual following upon any social network; and

         (f)  "Conveyance" means the voluntary, unconditional and gratuitous
              transfer to a Stranger of title to, and physical possession of,
              the Juice, at the sole cost and expense of the Licensee.

    1.2  Headings are inserted for convenience only and, like much else
         herein, shall not affect the construction of this Licence.

2.  GRANT

    Subject to, conditional upon and in consideration of the due performance
    of the obligation set forth in Clause 3, the Licensor hereby grants to
    the Licensee a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free licence
    to Use the Work, with or without modification, for any purpose whatsoever
    not being contrary to law.

3.  THE BEVERAGE OBLIGATION

    3.1  The Licensee shall, within a reasonable time of first Using the
         Work, and in any event not later than such time as the Licensee next
         finds itself in reasonable proximity to both a purveyor of Juice and
         a Stranger, effect not fewer than one (1) Conveyance.

    3.2  The obligation in Clause 3.1 shall not be discharged, nor deemed to
         have been discharged, by:

         (a)  a Conveyance to oneself, howsoever disguised;

         (b)  a Conveyance to any person who, by reason of that or any
              earlier Conveyance or otherwise, has ceased to be a Stranger;

         (c)  the tender of Juice which is unsealed, expired, tepid by
              design, or of a flavour which the Licensee knows or ought
              reasonably to know that no person would willingly accept; or

         (d)  any demand, express or implied, for reimbursement, reciprocity,
              gratitude in excess of the customary, or the Stranger's
              contact particulars.

    3.3  Nothing in this Licence shall oblige a Stranger to accept a
         Conveyance. Where a Conveyance is declined, the Licensee shall,
         without undue despondency, tender the Juice to the next available
         Stranger, and so on from Stranger to Stranger until accepted.

    3.4  The Licensee is not required to furnish to the Licensor any proof,
         receipt, photograph or sworn declaration of the Conveyance, the
         Licensor being content to rely upon the Licensee's conscience, which
         shall be the sole forum of competent jurisdiction in that regard.

4.  REDISTRIBUTION

    Any person redistributing the Work, in whole or in part and in whatever
    form, shall cause this Licence to accompany it, to the intent that each
    successive recipient shall become subject, severally and not jointly, to
    a Beverage Obligation of its own; and no recipient's Conveyance shall
    enure to the benefit of any other.

5.  EXCLUDED MATERIALS

    This Licence does not extend to materials of third parties distributed
    together with the Work, each of which remains subject to the terms under
    which it was made available, including without limitation the font file
    in assets/fonts/, which is governed by the IPA Font License Agreement
    v1.0 reproduced in that directory, and under which no Juice is owed.

